BAG-Piglet parameter-set implementation
=======================================

This directory is one self-contained BAG-Piglet security-strength instance.
The directory name selects the parameter set, and the exact constants are
defined in src/scheme/parameters.h. All tracked implementation and official
KAT sources are compiled as C11.

Directory layout
----------------

- CMakeLists.txt: C11 build configuration and target definitions
- Makefile: convenience targets for CMake
- doc/: Doxygen usage notes
- lib/api_pkc/: official auxiliary functions and deterministic RNG
- lib/randombytes/: operating-system random-byte interface
- src/common/: CCA-KEM, PKE, Gabidulin, parsing, and polynomial code
- src/scheme/: BAG-Piglet core operations and instance parameters
- src/ffi/: pointer-based finite-field interface used by the scheme
- src/rbc/: bundled RBC field, vector, space, polynomial, and quotient-ring code
- src/kat/KAT_KEM.c: official KAT driver
- src/kat/KEM_AlgorithmInstance.c/.h: permitted BAG-Piglet KAT adapter

Official KAT build
------------------

The default Make target builds only the official KAT:

    make

The explicit equivalent is:

    make kat

The executable name is derived from this directory:

    build/bin/<directory-name>-kat

For example, in bag_piglet128:

    ./build/bin/bag_piglet128-kat

The program writes its result to output/KAT_KEM_<algorithm-instance>.txt.
Expected vectors for all four security levels are stored in the repository's
top-level Test_Vectors directory.

Direct CMake build
------------------

To configure a formal build containing only the official KAT target:

    cmake -S . -B build -DBAG_PIGLET_BUILD_LOCAL_TESTS=OFF
    cmake --build build --target <directory-name>-kat -j

Replace <directory-name> with bag_piglet128, bag_piglet256, bag_piglet384, or
bag_piglet512.

Local-only test programs
------------------------

A developer checkout may retain the following ignored files:

- src/main_bag_piglet.c
- src/main_benchmark.c
- src/main_kat.c
- src/common/kem_bag_piglet.c
- src/common/kem_bag_piglet.h

They are not part of the remote repository or the official KAT. When the
functional and benchmark files exist locally, CMake discovers them and the
following convenience targets are available:

    make functional
    make benchmark

Official file boundary
----------------------

The official src/kat/KAT_KEM.c driver and lib/api_pkc files must remain
unchanged. Scheme-specific lengths and calls are connected through
src/kat/KEM_AlgorithmInstance.c/.h. The implementation uses bundled RBC
arithmetic and does not require NTL or OpenSSL; pthread is the only linked
system library beyond the C runtime.
